Description: Noble PDF Reader - High-performance Terminal & CLI PDF Swiss Army Knife
 Noble PDF Reader (created by MI_Syafaudin) is a blazing-fast, terminal-native
 PDF tool designed for Linux. It features a dual-mode interface: a scriptable
 POSIX CLI with clean exit codes and an interactive dual-pane Ratatui TUI
 with 24-bit TrueColor rendering.
 .
 Core capabilities include merge, split, extract, rotate, reorder, compress,
 text extraction, Tesseract OCR pipeline, bookmarks, and fast fuzzy navigation.
